# J17 — Updated PDF phase-cockpit reference
# Governing reference: /Users/operator/Desktop/Kuzushi TUI.pdf
# SHA-256: fad7e9bc324572ccf3e03b2e5c71878d1a6eba2795493f4a12005f0178a6f545
#
# The explicit DevEx hook enriches only the canonical offline-demo target with
# the same deterministic state used by the buffer contract. It cannot write
# into an operator target. `kuzushi demo` is the separate headless command, so
# this journey enters through the target gate and presses `d` inside the TUI.
# Numeric page keys are printable view hotkeys, so this journey enters strict
# Navigate mode before selecting Map, Hunt, Confirm, and Fix.
name: Updated PDF phase-cockpit reference (1a–1d)
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
keys: d
wait-for: 120 PDF phase reference fixture loaded
keys: Escape
submit: workbench
wait: 2
keys: F2
keys: 1
wait: 2
snap: 1a-map-recon
expect-ansi-profile: truecolor
expect: MAP
expect: TELEMETRY
expect: artifacts
expect: files 3
expect: dfd 3n/2f
expect: findings 6
expect: NEXT
ask: 1a Map — does the full-width trace/telemetry composition match the PDF hierarchy while every event, meter, cost, and NEXT action remains real or explicitly unavailable?
keys: 2
wait: 2
snap: 1b-hunt-split-cockpit
expect: HUNT
expect: SOURCE
expect: REVIEW QUEUE
expect: FINDINGS HEATMAP
expect: F-0001
expect: SQL injection
ask: 1b Hunt — does Source + Hunt + Review Queue sit above the spanning heatmap, with one clear selection and no fabricated queue or risk data?
keys: 3
wait: 2
snap: 1c-confirm-proof
expect: CONFIRM
expect: SQL injection reaches query
expect: ATTACK PATH
expect: DATA-FLOW LADDER
expect: PROOF · REPLAY
expect: replay verify-phase
expect: verify F-0001
ask: 1c Confirm — does the attack path lead into the source-to-sink ladder and proof sidecar, using PROOF · REPLAY only when a persisted replay artifact really exists?
keys: 4
wait: 2
snap: 1d-fix-breakdown
expect: FIX
expect: BREAKDOWN REPORT
expect: ATTACK TREE
expect: DFD
expect: REMEDIATION
expect: patch staged
expect: findings export report.sarif sarif
ask: 1d Fix — does the breakdown/report composition expose truthful totals, attack-tree/DFD evidence, remediation state, and a complete export action without imitating outer window chrome?
keys: Escape
